    {"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Audi maintenance cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An Audi oil service typically runs $130–$200 at an independent shop; the larger 40k major service costs more depending on model. S, RS and R8 engines hold more oil and run higher."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Audi service schedule?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most modern Audis use a 10,000-mile / 1-year oil-service interval, with a major inspection service around every 20,000–40,000 miles."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Is independent Audi service cheaper than the dealer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — typically 25–40% less for OEM-quality parts and the correct VW/Audi 502/504-spec oil, backed by our warranty."}}
